  "title": "ntlmssp, dcerpc-netlogin: Logging format truncation",
  "description": "snprintf always copies one less than the buffer size,\nbecause it ensures null termination. In that case, only putting\n3 for the bufsz here means unwanted truncation occurs. Just use\na wmem_strbuf, because it's harder to get that wrong and also\ncompilers are much less likely to complain about it for that reason.\n\nFixup f62e717a69a27c7d120dbcf81e5ce2613cd4fe74\nand e7ab91d072783beb5083a2db5e19fea834260e83\n\nThis one will trip with some clang versions, even without !17821\nmerged.\n\nPing #20175",
